{% import "_site.html.j2" as site with context %}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
{{ site.head("Updates · LLM Model Notes", "A dated log of new and materially revised pages on LLM Model Notes.", "/updates.html") }}
<body>
  {{ site.header("updates") }}
  <main id="main-content" tabindex="-1" class="prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Updates</p>
    <h1>Project log</h1>
    <p>New pages and substantive revisions are recorded here. Minor copy and styling corrections are not listed.</p>
    <p><a href="/feed.xml">Follow updates via Atom</a> for new and materially revised notes.</p>

    <div class="update-list">
      <article>
        <p class="meta"><time datetime="2026-11-04">4 November 2026</time></p>
        <h2>Open-weight models from Chinese labs</h2>
        <p>Added three notes: <a href="/notes/reading-an-open-weight-model-card.html">reading an open-weight model card</a>, <a href="/notes/serving-mixture-of-experts-models.html">serving mixture-of-experts models</a>, and <a href="/notes/tokenizer-efficiency-for-chinese-text.html">measuring tokenizer efficiency for Chinese text</a>. Published the <a href="/models.html">model tracker</a>, the <a href="/glossary.html">glossary</a>, and an <a href="/notes/">archive of all notes by topic</a>{% if nginx_xhttp_model_news_enabled | default(true) | bool %}, and started the automatically refreshed <a href="/news.html">news page</a>{% endif %}.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <p class="meta"><time datetime="2026-07-16">16 July 2026</time></p>
        <h2>Practical evaluation guides</h2>
        <p>Added three connected guides: <a href="/notes/reading-benchmark-results.html">reading benchmark results carefully</a>, <a href="/notes/latency-throughput-context.html">measuring latency, throughput, and context</a>, and <a href="/notes/repeatable-model-comparisons.html">building repeatable model comparisons</a>. Expanded the site scope and shared methodology.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <p class="meta"><time datetime="2026-07-12">12 July 2026</time></p>
        <h2>Initial reference pages</h2>
        <p>Published the project overview, comparison methodology, and introductory notes on benchmark interpretation and inference trade-offs.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
  {{ site.footer() }}
</body>
</html>
